---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Village Drill Hybrid | Community Transformation Trust" description="A portable Village Drill reaching remote communities in Sierra Leone and Liberia that larger rigs simply cannot access.">
  <div class="report-banner-wrap">
    <img class="report-banner" src="/images/water.png" alt="" loading="eager" />
  </div>
  <article class="wrap report-article">
    <h1>The Village Drill Hybrid</h1>
    <div class="detail-meta"><span>2023-2024</span><span>Sierra Leone &amp; Liberia</span></div>
    <p class="detail-lead">A portable, human-powered Village Drill is reaching remote communities in Sierra Leone and Liberia that larger rigs simply cannot access, bringing clean water to villages that have waited the longest.</p>

    <section class="reveal">
      <h3>Reaching the unreachable</h3>
      <p>Across Sierra Leone and Liberia, many remote communities are out of reach for the large drilling rigs that most water programmes depend on. Poor roads, difficult terrain, and high costs mean these villages are often left waiting the longest for clean water.</p>
      <p>The Village Drill Hybrid changes that. It can be transported to places heavy machinery cannot go, allowing skilled local teams to reach communities that would otherwise be overlooked.</p>
      <img class="report-photo" src="/images/water.png" alt="Portable Village Drill team at work" loading="lazy" />
    </section>

    <section class="reveal">
      <h3>Why the hybrid model works</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Portable enough to reach remote, road-poor communities.</li>
        <li>Lower cost per well than large mechanised rigs.</li>
        <li>Operated and maintained by trained local teams.</li>
        <li>Builds local capacity that continues drilling long after the first well.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="reveal">
      <h3>The lasting difference</h3>
      <p>Every new well is a source of health, dignity, and opportunity for a community that had none. By investing in a tool that reaches the hardest-to-serve places, this project extends clean water to families who need it most.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
